{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791025744,"nonce":"m5jUWIOoslG6mPDKHt0gU0Bq3dM=","title":"The side-module loader fills a module's own GOT.mem entries without its memory_base","message":"data_address (crates/ash_wasm_runtime/src/browser/dylink.rs and native/dylink.rs) answers a GOT.mem import with the value of the exported global of that name, the side module's first and then the program's. A side module's exported data symbols are offsets from its __memory_base (wasm-ld emits them relative without extended-const), so the entry should be memory_base + value; the program's are already absolute.\n\nIn hlwgpu's xgpu.wasm (dylink mem_size 32980), the side module's own GOT.mem imports are core's WHITESPACE_MAP (27498), OS_FUNCTIONS, std::alloc::HOOK, std::panicking::HOOK (32912) and panic_count::GLOBAL_PANIC_COUNT. Each resolves to that small absolute address in the program's memory instead of inside the module's data. GLOBAL_PANIC_COUNT is written on every unwind (a panic, or resume_unwind as hl_xidl's host::fail uses), so an unwind in a side module writes into whatever the program keeps there.\n\nhlwgpu's crates/hlwgpu/test/host/program.mjs, a host independent of Ash, adds memory_base for the side module's own symbols and only takes the program's (hlt_abstract) as is.","files":null}]}